# Its id leads with aspect-: a State of the same name (Raging, Mindful, God Ki) has the bare one.
id: aspect-pinnacle
name: Pinnacle
polarity: positive
levels: true
max: 2
# [Solo]: its levels are not added between Transformations used together - the highest of them.
solo: true
# number: its script is the whole of it. moment: entering, leaving, the start of a turn (stages 4-5).
# rule: how a Transformation is entered, left or Mastered - asked by transformations.mjs aspectLevel.
group: rule
# Its Transformation's own: it does nothing to the character in general - shown on its row, not among the Active Aspects (the user's).
bar: false
# The rule in short, for its hovers; its own words below (the page the user gave, 2026-11-20).
summary: >
  This Evolved Stage stacks on another Evolved Stage of the same Original Form. Level 2: you choose whether to apply it as you enter.
text: >
  Pinnacle [Solo, LV~2]: This Transformation can continue to evolve.
  –Effect: This Evolved Stage can be stacked atop another Evolved Stage with the same Original Transformation (for more information, see — Evolved Stages).

  If a Transformation has the 2nd level of the Pinnacle Aspect, you can choose whether to apply the Pinnacle Aspect or not when using the Transformation Maneuver to enter it.

---

# Nothing it does by itself yet: the Transformation Maneuver and Mastery read it.
